 🔹 We can enhance the capabilities of AI models by integrating external knowledge retrieval into the generation process.
 🔹 The goal of RAG is to produce more accurate, contextualized, and up-to-date outputs by augmenting generative models with retrieved knowledge from a database or knowledge repository.

📌 Key Components of RAG
🔹 A. Input Query
🔹 B. Retriever (Information Retrieval
     >>  🔹 The query is first processed by the Retriever, which helps search for most relevant and semantically related documents.
         🔹 Typically, retrieval is done via:
                 🎯 Embedding : means mathematical representation of words 
                 🎯 Vector database : designed to store embeddings
            🔹 Vector Search: Using embeddings to find semantically similar pieces of data.

     User query ---> embedding model --> Vector embedding  ---> Vector database
🔹 C. Arguementation
      >> Cleanup and retrive the retrived data
                 🎯 Filtering 
                 🎯 Ranking techniques
                     🔹 Semantic similarity
                     🔹 Retrival confidence score
                     🔹 Customized Ranking
                 🎯 Summarization
🔹 D. Generation
      >> The generative AI model (e.g., GPT or any transformer-based model) uses the query and the retrieved knowledge to generate a response.
         Unlike standalone generative AI, which relies solely on its trained knowledge, RAG supplements it with external information for a more informed and grounded response.


🔹 E . Data Injection Pipeline

